# Native approval protects execution, credentials, enforcement and core authority.
# Read alongside docs/autonomous-delivery.md: uncovered files still need
# content-based sensitivity assessment and the per-issue human-review choice.
# CODEOWNERS from the PR base applies; the last matching pattern wins.

# GitHub automation and merge enforcement
# Keep the ownership file, executable workflows/actions and their dependencies owned.
# Issue/PR templates have no blanket ownership.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @noofreuuuh
/.github/workflows/ @noofreuuuh
/.github/actions/ @noofreuuuh
/.github/requirements-ci.txt @noofreuuuh
/.github/dependabot.yml @noofreuuuh

# Contributor entrypoint, credential tooling and validation
# Skill Markdown is classified by its effects; bundled executable scripts stay owned.
/AGENTS.md @noofreuuuh
/.agents/**/scripts/ @noofreuuuh
/scripts/ci/ @noofreuuuh
/.gitleaks.toml @noofreuuuh
/.gitleaksignore @noofreuuuh

# Deployment and product runtime boundaries
# Retain these module-wide rules until real source layouts support narrower coverage.
# These paths are reserved by the architecture; they are not implemented packages yet.
/infra/ @noofreuuuh
/packages/policy/ @noofreuuuh
/packages/sandbox-manager/ @noofreuuuh
/packages/runtime/ @noofreuuuh
/packages/github/ @noofreuuuh

# Product skills: executable resources and explicit permission/promotion contracts
# Protect the current self-improvement entrypoint and promotion reference by name,
# rather than assigning every future skill document or asset to the owner.
/skills/**/scripts/ @noofreuuuh
/skills/jarvis-self-improvement/SKILL.md @noofreuuuh
/skills/jarvis-self-improvement/references/proposal.md @noofreuuuh

# Security, authority and governance contracts
# These documents define access, isolation, promotion or contributor approval rules.
/SECURITY.md @noofreuuuh
/docs/repository-security.md @noofreuuuh
/docs/development-github-app.md @noofreuuuh
/docs/autonomous-delivery.md @noofreuuuh
/docs/self-improvement-campaigns.md @noofreuuuh
/docs/common-agent-runtime.md @noofreuuuh
/docs/project-governance.md @noofreuuuh

# ADR indexes, templates and records have no blanket native ownership.
# Their decision/acceptance lifecycle remains in docs/project-governance.md.
# Changes to permissions, security or approval authority still need human review
# regardless of path; uncovered or declined optional review never waives that gate.
